Wed Aug  5 18:26:03 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Link the CPU kernels with -Wl,-z,noexecstack: the x86 variants
  (_C, _C_AVX2, _C_AVX512) pull in assembler objects that carry no
  .note.GNU-stack, so the linker marked the whole shared object's
  stack executable and rpmlint failed the build on it

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Aug  5 17:17:38 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Build vLLM's optimised C++ CPU kernels as a new "cpu" multibuild
  flavour (python-vllm-cpu, VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu), alongside the
  existing pure-Python default flavour:
  * The two flavours install the same importable vllm module, so the
    cpu one Conflicts with the default; install one or the other
  * The default flavour stays noarch and unchanged
- Bundle the sources the CPU kernels build from, since upstream's
  cmake/cpu_extension.cmake fetches them over the network at configure
  time, which an offline build root cannot do:
  * oneDNN, built statically, at upstream's two exact pins (a post-3.10
    snapshot on the aarch64/ACL path, the 3.10 tag on x86_64)
  * Arm Compute Library 52.6.0 as oneDNN's aarch64 backend, which
    upstream enables unconditionally when ASIMD is detected
  * Both are wired up through the FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_ONEDNN and
    ACL_ROOT_DIR environment overrides upstream already honours
- Add protobuf to BuildRequires: torch's Caffe2Config.cmake calls
  find_package(Protobuf) and hard-fails without it

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Jul 25 19:30:45 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.26.0:
  * New Inkling model family support including speculative
    decoding, LoRA and quantization; further new models:
    BertForMaskedLM, Roberta/XLMRoberta token classification,
    Cosmos3 Edge Reasoner, TranslateGemma-12b-it
  * DeepSeek-V4 performance push: specialized routing kernel,
    fused_topk_bias kernel, sparse decode/prefill optimizations
  * fp32 lm_head for generation models via head_dtype, also on
    the LoRA path
  * Attention backend selectable per KV-cache group and
    sliding-window support as an explicit backend capability
  * Matured KV offloading and tiered secondary storage:
    offloading metrics, object-store secondary tier,
    encoder-cache connectors with CPU offloading
  * Transformers 5.13 support with more models on the
    Transformers modeling backend
  * Requirements: diskcache and flashinfer-cubin dropped
- Rebase vllm-relax-cpu-requirements.patch onto the 0.26.0
  requirements (diskcache line removed upstream)
- Drop the python-diskcache runtime requirement accordingly

